ctor 0.4.3: support QNX (target_os = "nto") through .init_array

ctor knows its ELF targets by name and stops anywhere else with
"#[ctor]/#[dtor] is not supported on the current target". zenoh-c uses
#[ctor::ctor] on unix (src/lib.rs, ignoring SIGPIPE at load time), so
zenoh-c did not compile for QNX. QNX 8 is ELF and its runtime (crt1/ldd,
qcc's gcc 12) runs the .init_array entries of executables and shared
objects like the other ELF systems, so QNX joins the list of targets whose
constructors go into .init_array.

Upstream-Status: Pending
